  "id": "Compound::DB00786 - Gene::9313",
  "verbalization": "Marimastat is likely to interact with Mmp20 through a shared pathway involving matrix metalloproteinases (MMPs). The evidence suggests that Marimastat binds to Mmp23b, Mmp27, and Mmp26, all of which are part of the MMP family and are participated by Mmp20. This indicates that Marimastat may influence Mmp20 through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of MMPs. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent relationship, with Marimastat acting as a binder for multiple MMPs that are all associated with Mmp20. The integration of these pathways implies that Marimastat may exert its effects on Mmp20 through a general interaction with MMPs, potentially by inhibiting their activity or promoting their expression. The presence of multiple binding sites for Marimastat on different MMPs supports the idea that it acts as a broad inhibitor of MMPs, which in turn may affect Mmp20.",
